\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces Step-level wall time decomposition for CPU vs single-GPU at 10k, 50k, and 100k cells, mean of five repeats (first repeat included); the CPU and GPU panels have separate time axes. On CPU, DE testing and UMAP dominate; on GPU, the longest step, DE testing at 100k cells, takes 6.4 s on average. CPU neighbour search ran on one Numba thread, the Scanpy default (see Methods).}}{11}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:S1}{{S1}{11}{Step-level wall time decomposition for CPU vs single-GPU at 10k, 50k, and 100k cells, mean of five repeats (first repeat included); the CPU and GPU panels have separate time axes. On CPU, DE testing and UMAP dominate; on GPU, the longest step, DE testing at 100k cells, takes 6.4 s on average. CPU neighbour search ran on one Numba thread, the Scanpy default (see Methods)}{figure.1}{}}
