\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3.9}Spatial per-step speedup}{18}{subsection.3.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{spatial-per-step-speedup}{{3.9}{18}{Spatial per-step speedup}{subsection.3.9}{}}
\newlabel{tab:S7}{{S7}{18}{Spatial per-step speedup}{table.7}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S7}{Per-step wall time and GPU speedup on Visium HD 8~\textmu {}m (393,543 bins): mean~$\pm $~SD of five repeats, each in a fresh process; CPU reference: one DGX H100 node (100 CPUs); speedup: ratio of means with 95\% bootstrap interval. Spatial neighbours and neighbourhood enrichment have no GPU implementation in rapids-singlecell 0.14.1: the GPU pipeline calls Squidpy on the CPU, so the GPU column for these rows is CPU time on the workstation. PCA includes scaling. CPU expression neighbour search ran on one Numba thread (Methods). Co-occurrence: the GPU result with rapids-singlecell 0.14.1 was incorrect (see text), so no GPU time or speedup is reported (n.r.); with 0.15.1, in a separate check, it took 4.41 s (23.4$\times $). The total includes co-occurrence.}}{18}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
